            <ArticleTitle>Facilitated MIDCAB using a magnetic coupling device.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>691-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 59-year-old male with chronic occlusion of the left anterior descending coronary artery underwent a minimally invasive direct coronary artery bypass procedure using the second generation of a magnetic anastomotic coupling device. Postoperative angiogram demonstrated excellent patency and flow.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
